<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Petun</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tionontati, Tobacco Nation</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Petun, or Tionontati, were an Iroquoian people living south of Georgian Bay in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ontario">Ontario</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, neighbours and close allies of the Wendat. The French named them after the tobacco they grew. Dispersed by Iroquois attacks in 1649-1650, they merged with Wendat refugees to form the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wyandot">Wyandot</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/petun.jpg" alt="Petun" width="320" height="273" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Noahedits · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Petun_map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
